    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d415a42_4d8e4b53",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/UiccProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-31T23:42:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I made similar changes to areAllApplicationsReady()  and areAllRecordsLoaded(). But not exactly as \"return true only if mUiccApplications[0] \u003d\u003d null\". those methods will return true if all apps are ready, or  mUiccApplications[0] \u003d\u003d null (means no apps present).",
      "parentUuid": "6ac09909_05549f8b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 344,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "dd4de6655c07d5f57573e4ddd3e4b0f49889eedd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eab7143f_055f7050",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/UiccProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-31T23:49:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For that instead of directly returning true, you should return \"mUiccApplications[0] \u003d\u003d null\".\n\nThink of the scenario where there is only 1 app which is not supported. Then this and those functions will return different values. That is not an expected scenario, but still code wise we should be consistent in the return value in that case.",
      "parentUuid": "6d415a42_4d8e4b53",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 344,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "dd4de6655c07d5f57573e4ddd3e4b0f49889eedd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3eab1b83_d0a82e05",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/UiccProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-02-01T00:01:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "mUiccApplications[0] \u003d\u003d null definitely won\u0027t work, in normal cases, when all apps are ready/loaded, this function will never return true.\nIf there is one app which is not supported, we should directly return true because \"all supported apps\" is ready, so the logic here is clear. As for here, the only logic has been changed is that when there is no apps, we will try different logic, this won\u0027t affect the case when there is only 1 app but not supported, because this new branch is inside mUiccApplication \u003d\u003d null, we always return NOT_READY before/after this change.",
      "parentUuid": "eab7143f_055f7050",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 344,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "dd4de6655c07d5f57573e4ddd3e4b0f49889eedd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30051527_35cfe0e1",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/UiccProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-02-01T00:19:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure mUiccApplications[0] \u003d\u003d null won\u0027t work, and things will work fine in normal cases. But when there are only non-supported apps, or let\u0027s say just one app and it is not supported, then this code will return NOT_READY, whereas the ready/loaded functions will return true. Isn\u0027t that right, or am I missing something? I think we should not have this inconsistency.",
      "parentUuid": "3eab1b83_d0a82e05",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 344,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 44
      },
